course: dictionary
lesson: 4365
title: Gush: fast flow and too much praise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gush is a word you can use as a verb or a noun. When a liquid flows out suddenly, fast and in large amounts, it gushes. «On the dark sea floor, water gushes out of cracks in the rock.» The clues are cracks, hot rock and minerals, so gushes means the water bursts out fast, not that it drips slowly.
explain: A gush is the noun: a sudden, fast flow, as in «a gush of water». You can tell it is a noun because the word «a» comes before it. Read the words around gush to decide which meaning fits, the flow of a liquid or the praise.
explain: Gush has a second meaning. To gush about something is to praise it or be excited about it too much, in a way that can sound silly. If your aunt gushes over your drawing, she thinks it is brilliant and says so loudly. Ask yourself: is there a liquid in the sentence? If not, the praise meaning is likely.
fact: Gush means to flow out suddenly, fast and in large amounts.
fact: A gush is a sudden, fast flow, such as a gush of water.
fact: The verb forms are gushes, gushed and gushing.
fact: «Gushes» in the sea-floor sentence shows heated water pouring out of cracks, full of minerals.
fact: To gush about something means to praise it or get excited about it too much, in a way that can sound silly.
exercise: «Water, heated by hot rock deep below, gushes out of cracks on the dark sea floor.» What does gushes mean here? | *Flows out suddenly, fast and in large amounts | Sinks down quietly | Freezes into ice | Drips slowly, one drop at a time
exercise: Mia says, «Mum gushed about my drawing for ten minutes!» What does gushed mean? | *Praised it too much, in an excited, silly way | Drew a second picture | Threw it away | Whispered quietly about it
exercise: «A gush of water came out of the broken pipe.» What is a gush in this sentence? | A small sound | *A sudden, fast flow | A slow, dry leak | A kind of fish
test: «Water gushed from the broken pipe and flooded the road.» Which word is closest in meaning to gushed? | Trickled | Stopped | *Poured out fast | Dried
test: Sam says, «Grandma gushes about every cake I bake.» What does gushes mean? | Hides it | *Praises it too much, with too much excitement | Eats quickly | Bakes slowly
exam: «The hot water gushed out full of minerals.» Choose the best meaning of gushed. | Dried up slowly | Stayed still | Turned into smoke | *Flowed out suddenly and fast
